first_claim:
A method of controlling movement of a component (102) in a system (100) by a plurality of actuators (104), comprising:
 receiving an operation actuation command (200) to move the component (102); and 
 for each of the plurality of actuators (104):
 using the operation actuation command (200) to generate a feed-forward equalization command (142) for the actuator (114), 
 combining (140) the feed-forward equalization command (142) for the actuator (114) with the operation actuation command (200) to provide an equalized actuation command (152) for the actuator (114), and 
 controlling the actuator (114) to move the component (102) using the equalized actuation command (152) for the actuator (114).

